> After getting into the habit of throwing daggers, I seem to be
> accumulating so much that it weighs me down. So far in this game I have
> 26 uncursed daggers, 1 blessed dagger and 2 uncursed elven daggers.

I like about a dozen in my quiver.  Early on I get an assortment but
over time it boils down to a single stack.  Cancellation or whatever.
If you have 30, be sure to envhant them all together to the safe max
and drop the ones you aren't carrying.

It's a weight strategy issue more than anything.  Carry as many as
you can up to a point.  The more other gear you carry the fewer
daggers.  I like to carry enough that I can pick up a small variety
of items as I explore a new level, then drop all the new items at one
of the stairs.  The number of daggers seems to hover around dozen
for whatever reasons.  As the game processes and I carry more
armor and such, my strength goes up as well.

Type of dagger is a different issue.  Once you have a dozen total
daggers drop an orcish for each better one.  Once you have a
dozen combining regular and elven drop a regular with each new
elven that arrives.  Once you have a dozen elven drop an elven
for each new silver dagger that arrives if any ever do.  That plus
drop the cursed ones and such until you have a single stack.



